# The only files whose change may skip the heavy jobs of .github/workflows/ci.yml (see ci/changes.sh). One rule per line: <class> <bash glob>.
# `*` matches any characters, also `/`. A changed file that matches no line here means: run everything.
#
# Every line needs evidence that NO job of ci.yml reads, compiles, embeds or hashes the files it matches (the table is in CONTRIBUTING.md; the
# guard ci/skip-guard.sh greps for readers on every pull request and fails when one appears). Adding a line is a review decision: show the evidence.
#
# docs: the READMEs of the root and the documentation tree. No Go test, script, Makefile target, compose file or Dockerfile used by ci.yml opens them.
#       Only .md and .png under docs/ (docs/images/build.py is a script, so it is not listed). deploy/images/README.md is NOT here: ci/helm reads it.
docs README.md
docs README.zh-CN.md
docs CONTRIBUTING.md
docs DESIGN_SCALE.md
docs docs/*.md
docs docs/*.png
# chart: three Helm charts and the test tree ci/helm. ci.yml never runs helm; ci/helm is a separate Go module (not in `go test ./...` of the root
# module) that only .github/workflows/helm.yml and `make helm-check` run (the reviewed exception in ci/skip-module-exceptions).
# ci/kind is NOT here: a tree that is not in the repository cannot be proven safe, and the guard refuses a pattern that matches no tracked file. The kind
# lane's ci/kind/tools has Go code of the root module, which the `test` job compiles. Add a line for it, with evidence, in the pull request that has the files.
# deploy/helm/qv-certs is NOT listed: its catalog.json is read by a test of the root module (internal/pki/catalog_chart_test.go, the `test` job).
# Not a glob over deploy/helm/*: a new chart does not skip anything until someone checks it and adds it here.
chart deploy/helm/qv-business/*
chart deploy/helm/qv-party/*
chart deploy/helm/qv-signing-core/*
chart ci/helm/*
